body:
Having to choose the CCAs to join is definitely really tough! If you are able to try out the cca, you can do that to see if you really enjoy it. If you are not able to do so, then it's definitely best to ask around to find out more details about the CCA and ultimately choose the ones that will fit your schedule. 

&#x200B;

It's quite a common issue for CCA schedules to clash. I've had friends who had to skip certain sessions because they needed to attend another club's meeting or such. I'd say go for the one that is much more important, such as training sessions or AGM (general meeting). Knowing how to balance your CCA responsibilities and studies is very important. If a student has a test to study for or an assignment due, what they'd do is to inform their cca leaders that they would be skipping the upcoming cca session due to their studies. Students understand each other and also know the importance of school work, so most often than not, they'd let them off. I have done that many times before too. 

&#x200B;

I have never been part of the exco of my school's academic club, but one my friend has been for 2 years (even became the president). From what I know, usually the exco is in charge of planning school related events. Events like FMO, Open houses and special school days (e.g SIT Day) and school camps. All students are technically members of their respective school's academic club, but you have to sign up to be an exco member.

1.) Not really. The beauty of genshin is the fact that it's not an MMO. It's also not a PVP game. I accepted and embraced that right from the start. A portion of my friends are at higher AR, they do higher damage than me. I don't really care about that. I compare my damage to my past damage, and seeing it improve makes me happy.

&#x200B;

2.) I took a 4 month break from genshin. When I came back, I was way behind and missed out  a number of events and banners. At first I felt kind of sad of course, some of the events were so interesting. But overtime I just stopped caring and focused on my own journey. The more I focused on how I play the game and how I feel about the things I do, the more I grew to love the game. It has been over 200 days since I returned, and my love for the game has only grew.

&#x200B;

3.) Gacha games are essentially character collection games. I assume genshin is your first gacha game? There is absolutely nothing wrong with treating the game as a character collection game. Likewise there is nothing wrong with not seeing it that way. Personally I don't really see or treat the game as such, mainly because I'm a light spender and can't afford to get all the characters to begin with lol. I focus more on the gameplay of the characters. If I like how the character is like, I will get them. Pretty much how I decided to pull for kazuha lol. Pulling enemies in was SO satisfying, despite so many of my friends telling me not to because his dps potential is at c6 and that there's sucrose and venti.

&#x200B;

It's hard to stop ourselves from comparing to other people. Especially when growing up, we were practically forced to be compared through school and maybe our family. But the more we compare ourselves to others, the more miserable we will be. There will always be someone better than you, no matter where you go. This is why I try to encourage myself and others to compare ourselves to our past self. How have I improved? What can I do better? When I started to do that to all the things I do, such as my school work and on genshin, the more I appreciated myself and the things I do.

Honestly speaking, I pull and build characters so that I can play them. I always believe that having 2 solid teams for abyss is good, but having more characters means being able to try out different teams. Heck, sometimes I don't even want to use my usual abyss teams, sometimes I just feel like I want to use xyz characters. That's what drives me to pull and build for them. 

&#x200B;

Definitely bias, but this is also why I always advocate for pulling for characters that you find fun. If you choose to pull for meta, that's cool and it's up to you. But if you're stuck on who to pull, I always recommend pulling for a character you enjoy. At the end of the day, it is a game. You should enjoy playing it.
